      "message": "`slugify` now transliterates accented letters, so `café` becomes `cafe` instead of `caf`. All 5 tests in `tests/test_core.py` pass.\n\nThe cause was in `slug/core.py`: non-ASCII letters fell into an `elif ch.isalpha(): continue` branch and were silently dropped.\n\nChanges:\n- **`slug/core.py`**: Letters are decomposed with Unicode NFKD and the accent marks are dropped, so `é` becomes `e`. Letters that don't decompose (ß, æ, œ, ø, ł, đ, þ) use a small explicit map (`ß` → `ss`, `æ` → `ae`, and so on). Non-letter symbols such as `—` still become `-`, as before.\n- **`tests/test_core.py`**: Added three tests covering accented letters, the non-decomposing letters, and symbols still becoming dashes.\n\nLimitation: the map covers only the listed letters. Other scripts, such as Cyrillic or CJK, are still dropped. Say if you want broader coverage, for example via a transliteration library.\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
